    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d121">

                <pb facs="0367" n="53" xml:id="pg53"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/306</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Whitlock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-10T18:00:00+00:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 10, 1914, 6 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11:20 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>My colleague at The Hague informs me that memorandum referred to in my August 9,
                    6 [1] a.m. was authentic.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d121-f1"/> I learn quite
                    confidentially from the Foreign Office, however, that text has been presented to
                    the Belgian Government by an individual requested to do so by the Netherlands
                    Government. Answer indignantly rejecting it is now being prepared.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d121-f2"/> We are thus spared further embarrassment and the subject
                    is disposed of so far as we are concerned.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitlock</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
